pack_bytes

This function pack_bytes is designed to pack an array of bytes into individual bits in the m_bits array.

```systemverilog
function void uvm_packer::pack_bytes(ref byte value[], input int size = -1);
   int max_size = value.size() * $bits(byte);

   if (size < 0)
     size = max_size;

   if (size > max_size) begin
      `uvm_error("UVM/BASE/PACKER/BAD_SIZE",
                 $sformatf("pack_bytes called with size '%0d', which exceeds value size of '%0d'",
                           size,
                           max_size))
      return;
   end
   else begin
      // idx_select is used to determine which byte and bit to access, considering the endianness.
      // value[idx_select / $bits(byte)] selects the byte from the input array.
      // [idx_select % $bits(byte)] selects the specific bit within that byte.
